1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,040
Church would be known for its love, for your God, and it's in your son's name I pray, amen.

2
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:10,040
You can be seated.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:48,340
I'm still Kent McKay.

4
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:52,740
I'm still glad to be with you, and you're still at Canvas Community Church.

5
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:55,720
So, good morning.

6
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:58,520
Let me get this, I've got to get my Bible out.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,840
I don't know if you guys still use the traditional paper Bible.

8
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:05,600
Yeah, you do, huh?

9
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:18,500
And last week, Ryan came and talked to us about the early second chapter of Acts, the church there, as it was a new community that was forming,

10
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:22,760
and kind of drew parallels to where we are as a group together, right?

11
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:28,420
And this week, he asked me to come forward and talk about that, what that looks like as an individual.

12
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:32,680
Obviously, as a group, we're a body that's authentic and consistent and invested is what we want to be.

13
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:35,200
And as an individual, how does that, how do you fit in?

14
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:38,740
Where do my giftings and my calling, how does that fit into all that?

15
00:01:38,740 --> 00:01:40,600
So, that was what we wanted to talk about today.

16
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:50,100
And as we turn to that very personal topic, I want to turn to the words of a well-known sage, Shel Silverstein.

17
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:53,980
So, a wonderful poem he wrote.

18
00:01:53,980 --> 00:02:02,820
Lester was given a magic wish by the, Lester was given a golden wish by the goblin who lives in a banyan tree.

19
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:05,380
Sound good so far?

20
00:02:05,380 --> 00:02:06,540
All right.

21
00:02:06,540 --> 00:02:10,360
And with that wish, he simply wished for three more wishes.

22
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:16,640
So now, instead of just one wish, he cleverly had three.

23
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:22,200
And with each of these wishes, he simply wished for three more wishes, which gave him three old wishes plus nine new.

24
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:27,580
And with each of these twelve, he slyly wished for three more wishes, which added up to forty-six, thirty-six, fifty-two.

25
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:33,860
Well, anyway, he used each wish to wish for wishes until he had five billion, seven million, eighteen thousand, thirty-four.

26
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:37,440
And then he spread them on the ground and clapped his hands and danced around and skipped and sang.

27
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:40,280
And then sat down and wished for more and more and more.

28
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:41,000
And more they multiplied.

29
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:51,560
While other people laughed and cried and touched and reached and felt, Lester sat amidst his wealth, stacked mountain high like sacks of gold.

30
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:54,060
He sacked and counted and grew old.

31
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:57,900
And then one Thursday night, they found him dead with his wishes piled around him.

32
00:02:57,900 --> 00:03:00,760
And they counted a lot and found that not a single one was missing.

33
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:02,900
All shiny and new.

34
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:04,780
Here, take a few and think of Lester as you do.

35
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:09,840
In a world full of kisses and apples and shoes, he wasted his wishes on wishes.

36
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:14,580
And I think we've all been there.

37
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:16,000
There's a certain understanding in there.

38
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,680
There's a certain carpe diem.

39
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:19,860
Don't waste the golden gifts that you've been given.

40
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:21,700
Everybody immediately understands that.

41
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:22,780
And it's true.

42
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:29,420
I think it's so true, it's such a given, that a lot of times we read that into Scripture, right?

43
00:03:29,420 --> 00:03:33,380
A really good example is the parable of the talents from Matthew.

44
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:43,260
As a refresher, the parable is that there's a ruler who's going on vacation, going to a distant land.

45
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:44,020
We don't know what he's doing.

46
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:49,360
And he leaves a big pile of money to one servant, and a small pile to another servant, and a tiny little bit to a third servant.

47
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:53,680
And the third servant, instead of investing the money, buries it because he doesn't want to lose it.

48
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:54,420
He acts out of fear.

49
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:57,400
And the master says, no, no, no.

50
00:03:57,400 --> 00:04:01,640
You're supposed to invest and make the most of the golden gift that I gave you.

51
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:22,800
And that is, that sermon that I just gave you, that allegorical version of that parable where don't waste the gift you've been given, was preached so often, starting around 1500, about the time of the Reformation, that we have actually changed the word talent, which was a measurement, to a gifting.

52
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:27,080
That shift in the eating actually came from that sermon being preached constantly, right?

53
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:29,800
So a talent was actually a pile of money.

54
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:35,940
In the ancient world, a talent talentin, the Greek word actually means the scale that you've seen, the old scale they had in the marketplace.

55
00:04:35,940 --> 00:04:39,840
And a full dish was a talent, right?

56
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:40,720
It was a big old pile of money.

57
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:45,260
And, of course, the size of the dish and the money having it changed over time, so the value of the talent changed.

58
00:04:45,260 --> 00:04:51,960
But it was always sort of the expression used in the ancient world for, like we would say, if you win the lottery or a million dollars, right?

59
00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:53,080
It was just a big pile of money.

60
00:04:53,080 --> 00:04:54,300
That's what talent means.

61
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:56,240
And that's what Christ was talking about when he preached that parable.

62
00:04:56,240 --> 00:05:02,480
He's talking about the obedience of following through and making what you've been given multiply specifically for disciples, right?

63
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:03,720
Growing more disciples.

64
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,580
Acting while the master's away.

65
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:09,660
We simplified that down to don't waste the gift you've been given.

66
00:05:09,660 --> 00:05:13,180
And while that's not wrong, it's not the whole story, right?

67
00:05:13,180 --> 00:05:20,200
So what I want us to do today is take that understanding of a gift that's been given to us.

68
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:28,840
And it's true, but we just want to wrap it up and set it off to the side and read with new eyes some of what's said in Scripture, particularly in Ephesians, about our gifts and our callings.

69
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:29,040
Okay?

70
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:30,100
Sound good?

71
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:31,300
All right.

72
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:36,920
So in Ephesians, Paul has just spent the first three chapters.

73
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:39,820
And I've paraphrased it here in the Kent paraphrase.

74
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:45,580
I, Paul, am so dedicated to this mission that it's taken over my life and my health and my freedom.

75
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:46,280
And I'm now in prison.

76
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:50,840
And I pray daily that y'all will know God so deeply that you'll want to do the same thing.

77
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:53,960
And then the church will be vibrant with God's glory.

78
00:05:53,960 --> 00:05:57,580
Therefore, chapter 4, right?

79
00:05:57,580 --> 00:06:01,360
So he spent three chapters talking about what should happen.

80
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:03,040
And now he's going to tell you how to make it happen.

81
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:05,620
He's going from theory to action right here with the therefore.

82
00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:11,900
And what he says is, let's see.

83
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:13,080
Yeah, it changed.

84
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:17,960
I, therefore, am a prisoner of the Lord, because he's actually a prisoner for acting for the Lord.

85
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:21,620
I urge you to walk in a manner worthy of the calling into which you've been called.

86
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:24,100
Now, notice, he's just said, I'm going to tell you what to do.

87
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:25,060
And he doesn't tell us what to do.

88
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:26,340
He tells us how to do it, right?

89
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:28,760
The manner you're doing it, not where to walk, how to walk.

90
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:34,640
The manner in which you've been called, walk worthy of the calling in which you've been called,

91
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:38,640
with all humility and gentleness, with patience, bearing with one another in love,

92
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:41,700
eager to maintain the unity of the Spirit and the bond of peace.

93
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:42,560
This is great stuff.

94
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:44,240
Staying together.

95
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:44,720
Unity.

96
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:45,540
Bond of peace.

97
00:06:47,380 --> 00:06:52,420
There's one body and one Spirit, just as you were called into the one hope that belongs to your call.

98
00:06:52,420 --> 00:06:58,340
One Lord, one faith, one baptism, one God and Father of all, who is over all and through all and in all.

99
00:06:58,340 --> 00:07:02,040
But grace was given to each one of us according to the measure of Christ.

100
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:05,100
So, what's the first thing you notice about that passage?

101
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:07,420
How many times did you say the word one?

102
00:07:07,420 --> 00:07:09,200
Eight.

103
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:10,220
Good guess.

104
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:11,020
Unity, oneness.

105
00:07:11,020 --> 00:07:12,940
There's unity of the Spirit.

106
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:16,020
There's one body, one Spirit, one hope, one Lord, one faith, one path.

107
00:07:16,020 --> 00:07:17,120
And what do you think he's trying to tell them?

108
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:19,040
You're one unit, right?

109
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:20,400
You're one.

110
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:22,200
You're not acting like you're one.

111
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:23,180
That's what I'm writing to you about.

112
00:07:23,180 --> 00:07:23,740
But you're one.

113
00:07:23,740 --> 00:07:35,920
In our context, by the way, I think if we see our church as two groups come together to do something great,

114
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:37,960
we'll have missed the boat, right?

115
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:40,680
This is not two groups.

116
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:41,520
This is one body.

117
00:07:46,640 --> 00:07:52,300
It was one body specifically with one calling, right?

118
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:56,960
Men are worthy of a calling which you can call bearing with one another in love.

119
00:07:56,960 --> 00:07:59,340
You're to maintain the unity of the Spirit and the bond of peace.

120
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:03,180
There is one body and one Spirit just as you were called into the one hope that belongs to your calling.

121
00:08:03,180 --> 00:08:03,820
It's one thing.

122
00:08:06,180 --> 00:08:07,740
And Paul is a pun a minute.

123
00:08:07,740 --> 00:08:10,680
I don't know if you're familiar with Paul, but he's always using wordplay.

124
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:18,100
And when he says, I urge you to walk in a manner, the Greek word echaleo there is actually I call out to you.

125
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:22,040
It's I urge you in the same way I might urge you to look out there's a bus coming, right?

126
00:08:22,740 --> 00:08:25,680
Like, you know, English suffers from understatement.

127
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:31,000
And when he's urging you, he is screaming, there's a bus, get out of the way, right?

128
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,960
That's the level of urging we're talking about.

129
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:34,340
It doesn't translate so well.

130
00:08:34,340 --> 00:08:39,260
So I'm going to, again, change it to I call out to you, which is actually literally what he said.

131
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:42,680
I call out to you to walk in a manner worthy of a calling in which you've been called.

132
00:08:42,680 --> 00:08:44,780
He's emphasizing your call, right?

133
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:51,180
I'm calling out to you to remember the calling that you were called in to do it together, oneness, oneness, oneness, oneness, oneness.

134
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:52,240
Your calling is a unity.

135
00:08:52,240 --> 00:09:05,340
Calling is another word that we poured a new meaning into at about the same time for about the same reason.

136
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:09,500
At the time of the Reformation, the church had become a professional effort.

137
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:14,120
And there was clergy, and there were people who attended the church.

138
00:09:15,220 --> 00:09:17,680
And the Reformers said, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

139
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:19,800
You do church when you go home.

140
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:21,000
You take Christ with you.

141
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,020
You work all week long.

142
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:26,940
If you're a plumber, you take your calling to be a disciple home, and you do it while you're plumbing.

143
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:32,480
Paul, when he wrote this, was speaking to slave or free, circumcised or uncircumcised.

144
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:33,160
You're all the same.

145
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:34,520
You all have the same calling.

146
00:09:34,520 --> 00:09:39,920
The Reformers took this and said, if you're a nobleman or a tradesman, if you're a clergy or a peasant,

147
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:43,000
all of you follow God when you go home.

148
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,380
Do it all week long, right?

149
00:09:44,940 --> 00:09:48,900
And Paul specifically in 1 Corinthians 7.20?

150
00:09:48,900 --> 00:09:49,520
Yes.

151
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:55,400
It says, each one should remain in the condition you were called, that you were working in when you were called, right?

152
00:09:55,400 --> 00:10:01,500
So the condition you were working in means, no, no, no, you don't quit and you'll be a preacher because you accepted Christ and become a disciple.

153
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:05,300
Christ called you where you were so you could reach the people where you were, right?

154
00:10:05,300 --> 00:10:07,220
Where you are is where you should function.

155
00:10:07,220 --> 00:10:13,280
So, but because the calling in which you're called, because that sermon was preached so often in the Reformation,

156
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:16,660
we've ported the word sort of vocation into calling, right?

157
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:21,580
And your calling, not necessarily vocation, right?

158
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:23,000
That's a misalignment.

159
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:35,000
The disciples were very, very clear on the specific meaning of calling in their life because they had one by one stood still and heard the same voice that created the world.

160
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:44,420
In the beginning, God created, it was the word and the word was with God and all things were made by him and nothing was made without him that hasn't been made.

161
00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:45,680
It was first Christ.

162
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:48,400
And Christ called out to them and said, follow me.

163
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:52,400
And that living, luminous, creative word called out to them, come be my disciple.

164
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:54,280
And that is not a call you forget.

165
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:59,840
That noise, that voice that created the world coming to you and saying, be with me, learn from me, be my disciple.

166
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:01,840
That's a thing you don't forget.

167
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:05,320
That is a, it takes on a life of its own and that is your calling, the moment you were called.

168
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:12,020
And Paul is calling out to them to remember that moment of calling in which they were called because they, the Ephesians, like us,

169
00:11:12,020 --> 00:11:16,480
if they've decided to follow and be a disciple of Christ, have heard that voice in some way.

170
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:21,400
Maybe not as physically as Peter did on the shores of Galilee, but you have heard it and you've responded to it.

171
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:24,260
And that's why you're a disciple in this congregation today.

172
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:26,900
You're following the call to be a disciple.

173
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:36,200
And throughout the New Testament, they explained to, in these letters, obviously, I've said this before,

174
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:41,560
but there were probably thousands of letters that bishops wrote to churches saying,

175
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:45,260
that everything's well, hope everybody's doing well.

176
00:11:45,260 --> 00:11:50,300
But we kept the ones that were like, people are drunk at communion and there's incest because those are really interesting.

177
00:11:50,420 --> 00:11:51,520
How do you deal with those problems?

178
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:51,820
That's right.

179
00:11:51,820 --> 00:11:56,660
There were problems in the church among people trying to be disciples.

180
00:11:56,660 --> 00:12:01,200
And the apostles and the bishops were always writing to them saying, no, no, here's how you do it right.

181
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:06,700
And in doing that, they highlighted what it's like to be an apostle, what it's like to be a disciple when you're called.

182
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:12,120
And in Matthew 4 and Mark 1, of course, they talk about the physical calling to follow me.

183
00:12:13,740 --> 00:12:17,660
In 1 Corinthians 7, verse 15, it says, you've been called to peace.

184
00:12:17,660 --> 00:12:19,360
Is that a separate calling from being a disciple?

185
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:19,720
No.

186
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:22,040
That's an aspect of being a disciple of Christ.

187
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:28,460
If there's a choice between conflict and peace, if there's a choice between contention and peace, you choose peace.

188
00:12:28,460 --> 00:12:29,820
That's the path of the disciple.

189
00:12:29,820 --> 00:12:34,400
In Galatians, we're called to freedom versus legalism.

190
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:37,740
These people were trying to figure out how much of the law they had to follow.

191
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:41,460
And Christ said, no, no, as Paul said, as a disciple, you're called to freedom.

192
00:12:41,460 --> 00:12:43,000
You're called to peace.

193
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:43,620
You're called to freedom.

194
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:45,480
And here in Ephesians, we're called to unity.

195
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:46,720
That's part of being a disciple.

196
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:49,120
You can't be a proper disciple without being in unity.

197
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:53,960
In Colossians, we're called together into one body and in peace.

198
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:58,740
In 1 Thessalonians 4, we're called into sanctification, which is set apart for the work of God.

199
00:12:58,740 --> 00:12:59,760
We're called to be holy.

200
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:04,220
We are sanctified people, like the priests of old, right?

201
00:13:05,940 --> 00:13:09,320
In 1 Peter 1.15, you're called into holiness once again.

202
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:11,440
In Hebrews, into faithful obedience.

203
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:13,940
But these are not separate callings.

204
00:13:13,940 --> 00:13:15,680
This is all what it means to be a disciple.

205
00:13:15,680 --> 00:13:18,180
And this is what the apostles are telling us in the New Testament.

206
00:13:18,180 --> 00:13:21,840
In 1 Peter 2, this is one we like to skip, suffering.

207
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:22,780
We're called into suffering.

208
00:13:22,780 --> 00:13:25,700
Yeah, Christ suffered.

209
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:29,380
We're called into suffering with him because one body, one spirit, one God and Father.

210
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:33,720
We're called into his kingdom and to his glory in Thessalonians.

211
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:36,500
In 2 Thessalonians, again, called into the glory through the gospel.

212
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:39,280
In 2 Timothy, called into a holy calling.

213
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:48,100
Hebrews were promised an inheritance as part of that calling, as in those now brought into a sonship.

214
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:52,460
In 1 Peter 3, we inherit a blessing along with that.

215
00:13:52,460 --> 00:13:55,340
In 1 Peter 5, that blessing brings eternal glory.

216
00:13:55,340 --> 00:13:58,100
And in Revelations 19, we're called to the marriage supper of the Lamb.

217
00:13:58,100 --> 00:14:00,700
We're united with Christ in the end.

218
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:02,940
That is all the same calling.

219
00:14:02,940 --> 00:14:10,400
So, should you, as a teacher, Barrett, keep following God as a teacher?

220
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:11,460
Absolutely.

221
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:13,560
Is that your calling?

222
